---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Student walkthroughs" description="A bespoke, self-paced guide to building and publishing your portfolio with GitHub, VS Code, and Copilot.">
<div class="container student-guide">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Your workshop field guide · written to use in class or at home</div>
    <h1>Follow the steps.<br/>Build your site.</h1>
    <p>You do not need to know everything before you begin. Follow one step, check what you see, and move to the next. You can return to this guide after class.</p>
    <div class="guide-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="https://github.com/skyeshanohan/workshopsite/archive/refs/heads/portfolio-starter.zip">Download your portfolio starter ↓</a><a class="btn" href="#step-1">Start step 1</a><a class="btn" href={base+'designs/'}>Preview the 3 designs ↗</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-status card">
    <div><div class="eyebrow">Your progress</div><h2 id="guide-progress-label">0 of 6 steps complete</h2><p class="muted small">Your progress is saved in this browser on this device.</p></div>
    <div class="guide-progress"><div class="progress-wrap"><div class="progress-bar" id="guide-progress-bar"></div></div><span id="guide-progress-percent">0%</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-step" id="step-1" data-step="1">
    <div class="step-number">01</div><div class="step-content">
      <div class="step-kicker">START HERE · 10 MINUTES</div><h2>Get ready to build</h2>
      <p class="step-lede">You need three tools. Each one has a different job.</p>
      <div class="tool-cards"><article><b>GitHub</b><p>A website where your project and its history live.</p></article><article><b>VS Code</b><p>The editor where you open and change project files.</p></article><article><b>Copilot</b><p>An AI assistant that can explain code and suggest changes.</p></article></div>
      <div class="plain-note"><b>Useful words</b><p><strong>Repository (repo):</strong> your project files plus their history. <strong>Commit:</strong> a saved checkpoint. <strong>Publish:</strong> make the site available at a web address.</p></div>
      <div class="step-task"><span class="task-label">DO THIS</span><ol><li>Open your GitHub account in a browser.</li><li>Open VS Code on your computer.</li><li>In VS Code, check that the GitHub and Copilot accounts are the ones you plan to use.</li></ol><p class="help-text">If Copilot is not ready, keep going. You can follow the same steps without AI while the instructor helps.</p></div>
      <label class="step-done"><input type="checkbox" data-step-check="1"/> I can open GitHub and VS Code.</label>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-step" id="step-2" data-step="2">
    <div class="step-number">02</div><div class="step-content">
      <div class="step-kicker">YOUR PROJECT · 10–15 MINUTES</div><h2>Create your own repository</h2>
      <p class="step-lede">A repository is the home for your site. You will own this copy, so your changes will not affect another student.</p>
      <figure class="walkthrough-figure"><img src={base+'walkthroughs/github-create-repository.svg'} alt="Illustration of the GitHub new repository form with repository name, Public visibility, and Create repository button."/><figcaption>This is the shape of the form to look for. GitHub may change the exact wording or layout.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="step-task"><span class="task-label">DO THIS</span><ol><li>Download the <strong>portfolio starter ZIP</strong> using the yellow button near the top of this page.</li><li>Extract the ZIP file. Open the new folder that contains <code>package.json</code> and the <code>src</code> folder in VS Code.</li><li>On GitHub, choose <strong>New repository</strong>. Give it a simple name such as <code>my-resume-site</code>.</li><li>Choose <strong>Public</strong> only if you are comfortable with the source code and website being visible to anyone. A public site should contain only details you are happy to share.</li><li>Create the repository without adding a README, license, or .gitignore. The starter already has project files.</li><li>In VS Code's terminal, run the commands below from the starter folder. Replace the example username and repository name with yours.</li></ol><p class="help-text">Copy one command at a time. The terminal runs commands on your computer; GitHub's website is where you create the empty remote repository.</p></div>
<div class="command-grid">
 <div class="command-card"><div><b>1 · Start Git history</b><button class="copy-button" data-copy-command="cmd-init">Copy</button></div><pre id="cmd-init">git init</pre></div>
 <div class="command-card"><div><b>2 · Stage the project files</b><button class="copy-button" data-copy-command="cmd-add">Copy</button></div><pre id="cmd-add">git add .</pre></div>
 <div class="command-card"><div><b>3 · Make the first commit</b><button class="copy-button" data-copy-command="cmd-commit">Copy</button></div><pre id="cmd-commit">git commit -m "Create my portfolio"</pre></div>
 <div class="command-card"><div><b>4 · Name the main branch</b><button class="copy-button" data-copy-command="cmd-branch">Copy</button></div><pre id="cmd-branch">git branch -M main</pre></div>
 <div class="command-card"><div><b>5 · Connect your GitHub repository</b><button class="copy-button" data-copy-command="cmd-remote">Copy</button></div><pre id="cmd-remote">git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPOSITORY.git</pre><p class="help-text">Change both capitalized placeholders first. Use the HTTPS URL shown on your repository page.</p></div>
 <div class="command-card"><div><b>6 · Send your files to GitHub</b><button class="copy-button" data-copy-command="cmd-push">Copy</button></div><pre id="cmd-push">git push -u origin main</pre></div>
</div>
      <div class="plain-note"><b>Why this matters</b><p>Your own repository means you can change the site, keep a history, and publish it under your own account or organization.</p></div>
      <label class="step-done"><input type="checkbox" data-step-check="2"/> I have a repository for my own portfolio.</label>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-step" id="step-3" data-step="3">
    <div class="step-number">03</div><div class="step-content">
      <div class="step-kicker">OPEN THE CODE · 10 MINUTES</div><h2>Open it in VS Code</h2>
      <p class="step-lede">GitHub stores the shared copy. VS Code lets you work on the files on your computer.</p>
      <figure class="walkthrough-figure"><img src={base+'walkthroughs/vscode-source-control.svg'} alt="Illustration of VS Code Source Control showing changed files, a commit message box, a Commit button, and code differences."/><figcaption>Look for the Source Control icon and the list of changed files. This is an illustration, not a screenshot from your exact version.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="step-task"><span class="task-label">DO THIS</span><ol><li>In VS Code, open the folder that contains <code>package.json</code> and the <code>src</code> folder.</li><li>Open the integrated terminal: <strong>Terminal → New Terminal</strong>.</li><li>Install the starter's packages with <code>npm install</code>. This downloads the tools the project uses.</li><li>Start a local preview with <code>npm run dev</code>.</li><li>Open the local address printed in the terminal, usually <code>http://localhost:4321</code>.</li></ol><p class="help-text">Leave the terminal running while you preview the site. The local address works on your computer; it is not the public website yet.</p></div>
<div class="command-grid command-grid-short">
 <div class="command-card"><div><b>Install project tools</b><button class="copy-button" data-copy-command="cmd-npm-install">Copy</button></div><pre id="cmd-npm-install">npm install</pre></div>
 <div class="command-card"><div><b>Start the local preview</b><button class="copy-button" data-copy-command="cmd-npm-dev">Copy</button></div><pre id="cmd-npm-dev">npm run dev</pre></div>
</div>
      <div class="prompt-card"><div class="prompt-heading"><div><span class="prompt-label">COPILOT PROMPT</span><h3>Ask Copilot to explain the files</h3></div><button class="copy-button" data-copy-prompt="explain-project">Copy prompt</button></div><pre id="explain-project">Explain this project in plain English. Tell me which file creates the page, which file controls the styles, and where I should edit my name, education, experience, skills, and projects. Do not change any files yet. Use short sentences.</pre></div>
      <div class="plain-note"><b>Read this before editing</b><p>It is okay if the code looks unfamiliar. First learn which file does what. Ask Copilot to explain; do not ask it to rewrite the entire project.</p></div>
      <label class="step-done"><input type="checkbox" data-step-check="3"/> I can open the project and preview it locally.</label>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-step" id="step-4" data-step="4">
    <div class="step-number">04</div><div class="step-content">
      <div class="step-kicker">MAKE IT YOURS · 20 MINUTES</div><h2>Choose a design and personalize it</h2>
      <p class="step-lede">Pick a design you like. Replace example content with information you want future employers or interviewers to see.</p>
      <div class="student-designs">
        <a href={base+'previews/editorial/'} class="student-design"><div class="design-swatch editorial-swatch"><small>01 / EDITORIAL</small><b>Thoughtful.<br/>By design.</b><i></i><i></i></div><strong>Editorial</strong><span>Warm, story-led, expressive.</span></a>
        <a href={base+'previews/developer/'} class="student-design"><div class="design-swatch developer-swatch"><small>02 / DEVELOPER</small><b>Build.<br/><em>Create_</em></b><i></i><i></i></div><strong>Developer</strong><span>Dark, technical, project-first.</span></a>
        <a href={base+'previews/professional/'} class="student-design"><div class="design-swatch professional-swatch"><small>03 / PROFESSIONAL</small><b>Jordan Lee</b><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><strong>Professional</strong><span>Structured, recruiter-friendly.</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="step-task"><span class="task-label">DO THIS</span><ol><li>Choose one design. You can change it later.</li><li>Update your name, short introduction, education, and skills.</li><li>Add one project. Class assignments are okay if you explain your contribution honestly.</li><li>Preview the page at desktop width and narrow/mobile width.</li><li>Check that your links point to the right places.</li></ol></div>
      <figure class="walkthrough-figure"><img src={base+'walkthroughs/copilot-prompt.svg'} alt="Illustration of Copilot Chat in VS Code with a focused portfolio prompt and an explanation of the proposed work."/><figcaption>Use Copilot Chat to ask a clear question. Your panel may look different, but the idea is the same: give context, request one change, and review the answer.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="prompt-card"><div class="prompt-heading"><div><span class="prompt-label">COPILOT PROMPT</span><h3>Make one small improvement</h3></div><button class="copy-button" data-copy-prompt="one-improvement">Copy prompt</button></div><pre id="one-improvement">I am building a student resume portfolio. Please make one focused improvement: [describe the change]. Keep the existing Astro project structure and visual style. Do not add packages or rewrite unrelated files. First tell me which files you plan to change. After the change, explain what I should review and how to test it on mobile.</pre></div>
      <div class="plain-note"><b>Privacy check</b><p>Only publish details you are comfortable sharing publicly. Do not include your home address, passwords, API keys, private contact details, or information about another person without permission.</p></div>
      <label class="step-done"><input type="checkbox" data-step-check="4"/> My site includes my own information and at least one project.</label>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-step" id="step-5" data-step="5">
    <div class="step-number">05</div><div class="step-content">
      <div class="step-kicker">SAVE A CHECKPOINT · 15–20 MINUTES</div><h2>Commit a change and open a pull request</h2>
      <p class="step-lede">A commit records a checkpoint. A pull request lets you review a change before it joins the main version of your project.</p>
      <div class="mini-workflow"><span>Issue</span><b>→</b><span>Branch</span><b>→</b><span>Commit</span><b>→</b><span>Pull request</span><b>→</b><span>Merge</span></div>
      <div class="step-task"><span class="task-label">DO THIS</span><ol><li>On GitHub, open <strong>Issues</strong> and create a small task. Example: “Add a featured project card.”</li><li>Write a few checks that tell you when it is complete: a title, a short summary, a working link, and a layout that fits a phone screen.</li><li>Create a branch for this task. A branch is a separate line of work; it keeps this change organized.</li><li>Make the change in VS Code. Inspect the diff, then write a clear commit message.</li><li>Push the branch to GitHub and open a pull request.</li></ol></div>
      <figure class="walkthrough-figure"><img src={base+'walkthroughs/github-pull-request.svg'} alt="Illustration of a GitHub pull request page with a branch comparison, changed lines, review checklist, and merge button."/><figcaption>The pull request is where you check the actual changes before merging them.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="prompt-card"><div class="prompt-heading"><div><span class="prompt-label">COPILOT PROMPT</span><h3>Review your own change</h3></div><button class="copy-button" data-copy-prompt="review-change">Copy prompt</button></div><pre id="review-change">Review my current changes against these acceptance checks: [paste your checks]. Look for broken links, mobile layout problems, accessibility issues, accidental secrets, and unrelated edits. Explain any problems in plain English. Do not make more changes until I review your findings.</pre></div>
      <div class="plain-note"><b>Before you merge</b><p>Read the changed files. Make sure the change matches your issue. Do not merge only because a button is green or Copilot says it is finished.</p></div>
      <label class="step-done"><input type="checkbox" data-step-check="5"/> I recorded a change and reviewed a pull request (or followed the class checkpoint).</label>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-step" id="step-6" data-step="6">
    <div class="step-number">06</div><div class="step-content">
      <div class="step-kicker">PUBLISH · 15 MINUTES</div><h2>Publish with GitHub Pages</h2>
      <p class="step-lede">Your source code is the recipe. The build creates the ready-to-serve files. GitHub Pages serves those files as a website.</p>
      <div class="deploy-illustration"><article><span>01</span><b>Your repository</b><small>Astro source files</small></article><div>→</div><article><span>02</span><b>GitHub Actions</b><small>Install + build</small></article><div>→</div><article><span>03</span><b>GitHub Pages</b><small>Live website</small></article></div>
      <figure class="walkthrough-figure"><img src={base+'walkthroughs/github-pages.svg'} alt="Illustration of repository Settings with Pages selected, source set to GitHub Actions, and a workflow success card."/><figcaption>For this workshop, Pages uses GitHub Actions as its publishing source.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="walkthrough-figure"><img src={base+'walkthroughs/github-actions-run.svg'} alt="Illustration of a successful GitHub Actions build and deployment, including checkmarks for installing dependencies, building the site, and deploying."/><figcaption>Look for a successful build and a successful deploy. Then open the actual website URL and test it.</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="step-task"><span class="task-label">DO THIS</span><ol><li>On your repository, open <strong>Settings</strong>, then <strong>Pages</strong>.</li><li>Under the publishing source, choose <strong>GitHub Actions</strong> when instructed by your starter setup.</li><li>Open the <strong>Actions</strong> tab and find the latest “Build and deploy” run.</li><li>Wait for the build and deployment steps to finish successfully.</li><li>Open the published URL. Check the homepage, one project link, and the mobile layout.</li></ol><p class="help-text">The first deploy can take a few minutes. If it fails, open the run and read the first error before changing anything.</p></div>
      <div class="prompt-card"><div class="prompt-heading"><div><span class="prompt-label">COPILOT PROMPT</span><h3>Understand a deployment error</h3></div><button class="copy-button" data-copy-prompt="debug-deployment">Copy prompt</button></div><pre id="debug-deployment">Help me understand this build/deployment error in plain English: [paste the error text]. Tell me which step failed, the likely cause, and the smallest safe fix. Do not guess at settings that are not shown in the log.</pre></div>
      <label class="step-done"><input type="checkbox" data-step-check="6"/> My published website opens, or I know exactly which deployment step needs help.</label>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="finish-card">
    <div class="eyebrow">You made it</div><h2>Your next change is easier.</h2><p>You now have a project you can keep improving. Workshop 2 will add automated checks and a more complete delivery pipeline. You do not need to memorize every term today; keep this guide and reuse the steps.</p>
    <div class="finish-links"><a class="btn primary" href={base+'workshop/'}>Return to workshop checklist ↗</a><a class="btn" href={base+'slides/'}>Open the presentation ↗</a></div>
  </section>
</div>
<style>
.student-guide{padding-bottom:70px}.guide-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-top:24px}.guide-status{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:25px;margin:0 0 38px;background:#fff;border-color:#d7d7d2}.guide-status h2{font:700 23px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif;margin:5px 0}.guide-status p{margin:0}.guide-progress{width:min(250px,35%);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;align-items:center;gap:10px}.guide-progress .progress-wrap{grid-column:1/-1;width:100%}.guide-progress>span{grid-column:2;font:700 12px 'Roboto',sans-serif}.guide-step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:65px minmax(0,1fr);gap:25px;padding:37px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:25px}.step-number{font:700 26px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif;width:55px;height:55px;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#FFDB00;color:#000;border-radius:4px}.step-content{min-width:0;max-width:920px}.step-kicker{font:700 10px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;color:#5e5e5e}.step-content h2,.finish-card h2{font:700 clamp(27px,4vw,39px)/1.1 'Titillium Web',sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:8px 0 12px}.step-lede{font:17px/1.6 'Roboto',sans-serif;color:#555;max-width:760px;margin:0 0 22px}.tool-cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:12px;margin:17px 0}.tool-cards article{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:17px}.tool-cards b{font:700 16px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif}.tool-cards p{font:13px/1.55 'Roboto',sans-serif;color:#555;margin:5px 0 0}.walkthrough-figure{margin:20px 0 25px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:12px}.walkthrough-figure img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:8px}.walkthrough-figure figcaption{font:12px/1.5 'Roboto',sans-serif;color:#666;padding:10px 5px 3px}.step-task{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:13px;padding:20px 22px;margin:18px 0}.task-label,.prompt-label{font:700 10px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.13em;color:#555}.step-task ol{padding-left:24px;margin:13px 0 0}.step-task li{font:14px/1.75 'Roboto',sans-serif;color:#222;padding-left:4px;margin:4px 0}.step-task strong{font-weight:700}.step-task code,.plain-note code{font:12px 'DM Mono',monospace;background:#f0f0ec;border:1px solid #d7d7d2;border-radius:4px;padding:2px 5px}.help-text{font:12px/1.6 'Roboto',sans-serif!important;color:#666!important;margin:13px 0 0!important}.plain-note{border-left:4px solid #FFDB00;background:#efefeb;padding:15px 18px;margin:17px 0;border-radius:0 9px 9px 0}.plain-note>b{font:700 13px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif}.plain-note p{font:13px/1.65 'Roboto',sans-serif;color:#444;margin:5px 0 0}.command-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px;margin:15px 0 18px}.command-card{border:1px solid #d7d7d2;border-radius:10px;background:#fff;padding:13px;min-width:0}.command-card>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:8px}.command-card b{font:700 12px Titillium Web,sans-serif}.command-card pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:11px/1.6 DM Mono,monospace;background:#f2f2ef;padding:10px;border-radius:6px;margin:10px 0 0}.command-card .copy-button{padding:7px 9px}.command-grid-short{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.step-done{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:10px;padding:14px;border:1px solid #d2d2cb;background:#fff;border-radius:10px;font:600 13px/1.55 'Roboto',sans-serif;margin-top:20px;cursor:pointer}.step-done input{accent-color:#000;width:18px;height:18px;flex-shrink:0;margin:1px 0 0}.prompt-card{border:1px solid #d5d5d0;background:#fff;border-radius:13px;padding:17px;margin:18px 0}.prompt-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:15px;align-items:center}.prompt-heading h3{font:700 17px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif;margin:4px 0}.copy-button{background:#000;border:1px solid #000;color:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:9px 12px;font:700 11px 'Roboto',sans-serif;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap}.copy-button:hover{background:#FFDB00;color:#000}.prompt-card pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:#f3f3ef;border:1px solid #deded8;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;font:12px/1.7 'DM Mono',monospace;color:#222;margin:12px 0 0}.student-designs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:12px}.student-design{text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);background:#fff;border-radius:12px;padding:12px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px}.student-design:hover{border-color:#777}.student-design strong{font:700 16px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif}.student-design>span{font:12px/1.5 'Roboto',sans-serif;color:#666}.design-swatch{height:155px;padding:12px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px;overflow:hidden}.design-swatch small{font:8px 'DM Mono',monospace}.design-swatch b{font:700 24px/1 'Titillium Web',sans-serif}.design-swatch i{height:4px;display:block;width:85%;background:#bbb}.design-swatch i:nth-last-child(1){width:55%}.editorial-swatch{background:#f4f0e5;color:#111}.editorial-swatch b{font:400 27px/1 Georgia,serif}.developer-swatch{background:#111;color:#fff}.developer-swatch em{color:#FFDB00;font-style:normal}.developer-swatch i{background:#c5e85a}.professional-swatch{background:#edf1f6;color:#111}.professional-swatch b{font-size:21px}.professional-swatch i{background:#c0cad7}.mini-workflow{display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:15px;background:#111;border-radius:10px;color:#fff;margin:17px 0}.mini-workflow span{background:#fff;color:#111;padding:9px 12px;border-radius:5px;font:700 12px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif}.mini-workflow span:first-child,.mini-workflow span:last-child{background:#FFDB00}.mini-workflow>b{color:#FFDB00}.deploy-illustration{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 30px 1fr 30px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin:20px 0}.deploy-illustration article{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px;padding:15px;border:1px solid #d7d7d2;background:#fff;border-radius:10px}.deploy-illustration article>span{background:#FFDB00;color:#000;width:25px;height:25px;display:grid;place-items:center;font:700 11px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif}.deploy-illustration b{font:700 15px 'Titillium Web',sans-serif}.deploy-illustration small{font:12px 'Roboto',sans-serif;color:#666}.deploy-illustration>div{text-align:center;font-size:21px;color:#777}.finish-card{background:#000;color:#fff;padding:clamp(25px,5vw,50px);border-radius:16px;margin:40px 0 0}.finish-card .eyebrow{color:#FFDB00}.finish-card p{font:15px/1.7 'Roboto',sans-serif;color:#ddd;max-width:760px}.finish-links{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:20px}.finish-links .btn:not(.primary){color:#fff;border-color:#555}.finish-links .btn:not(.primary):hover{color:#000}
@media(max-width:650px){.guide-status{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}.guide-progress{width:100%}.command-grid,.command-grid-short{grid-template-columns:1fr}.guide-step{grid-template-columns:42px 1fr;gap:12px;padding:28px 0}.step-number{width:38px;height:38px;font-size:19px}.tool-cards,.student-designs{grid-template-columns:1fr}.design-swatch{height:180px}.deploy-illustration{grid-template-columns:1fr}.deploy-illustration>div{transform:rotate(90deg)}.step-task{padding:15px}.walkthrough-figure{padding:6px}.prompt-heading{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}.mini-workflow{gap:6px}.mini-workflow span{font-size:10px;padding:7px 8px}}
</style>
<script>
const checks=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-step-check]')];
const storageKey='mis-workshop-student-walkthrough';
try{const saved=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(storageKey)||'{}');checks.forEach(c=>c.checked=!!saved[c.dataset.stepCheck])}catch{}
function updateGuideProgress(){const done=checks.filter(c=>c.checked).length;const pct=Math.round(done/checks.length*100);document.querySelector('#guide-progress-label').textContent=done+' of '+checks.length+' steps complete';document.querySelector('#guide-progress-percent').textContent=pct+'%';document.querySelector('#guide-progress-bar').style.width=pct+'%';try{localStorage.setItem(storageKey,JSON.stringify(Object.fromEntries(checks.map(c=>[c.dataset.stepCheck,c.checked]))))}catch{}}
checks.forEach(c=>c.addEventListener('change',updateGuideProgress));updateGuideProgress();
document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy-prompt]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',async()=>{const target=document.getElementById(button.dataset.copyPrompt);try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(target.textContent.trim());button.textContent='Copied ✓'}catch{const range=document.createRange();range.selectNodeContents(target);const selection=window.getSelection();selection.removeAllRanges();selection.addRange(range);button.textContent='Select text and copy'}setTimeout(()=>button.textContent='Copy prompt',1800)}));
document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy-command]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',async()=>{const target=document.getElementById(button.dataset.copyCommand);try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(target.textContent.trim());button.textContent='Copied ✓'}catch{const range=document.createRange();range.selectNodeContents(target);const selection=window.getSelection();selection.removeAllRanges();selection.addRange(range);button.textContent='Select text and copy'}setTimeout(()=>button.textContent='Copy',1800)}));
</script>
</BaseLayout>